      "instruction": "Build, find the mistake, fill in",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "1",
          "type": "build_sentence",
          "translation": "Before the chef arrived, we cleaned the kitchen.",
          "words": [
            "Şefin",
            "gelmesinden",
            "önce",
            "mutfağı",
            "temizledik."
          ],
          "distractors": [
            "gelmesindan",
            "itibaren"
          ],
          "explanation": "Owner şefin, action gelmesi, plus n and -den, then önce. The verb goes last."
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "type": "error_hunt",
          "prompt": "Find the mistake",
          "tokens": [
            "Benim",
            "gelmesinden",
            "sonra",
            "yemek",
            "başladı."
          ],
          "wrong": 1,
          "fix": "gelmemden",
          "options": [
            "gelmemden",
            "gelmenden",
            "gelmesinden"
          ],
          "explanation": "benim means “my.” So the owner in the word is “I” too: gelmemden."
        },
        {
          "id": "3",
          "type": "gap_fill",
          "text": "Dersin bit___ itibaren telefonlar açık.",
          "answers": [
            [
              "mesinden"
            ]
          ],
          "options": [
            [
              "mesinden",
              "mesiden",
              "menden"
            ]
          ],
          "translation": "From the end of class on, phones are on.",
          "explanation": "dersin — “of the class,” owner “its.” bit + me + si + n + den."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "c1.masindan-itibaren.ex4",
      "lesson": 1,
      "kind": "practice",
      "skill": "grammar",
      "type": "custom",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "instruction": "Merge the word to order",
      "description": "Merge kitchen: the learner taps pieces in order (verb, knife, owner, -dAn, timer), and they stick together into a word. A mistake means a shake and a hint. The logic lives in index.html.",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "1",
          "ru": "before he arrives",
          "lead": "onun",
          "pool": [
            "den",
            "gel",
            "si",
            "önce",
            "nden",
            "me"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "gel",
            "me",
            "si",
            "nden",
            "önce"
          ],
          "explanation": "gel + me + si + n + den + önce. After “his,” the buffer n."
        },
        {
          "id": "2",
          "ru": "after our return",
          "lead": "bizim",
          "pool": [
            "ünüz",
            "dön",
            "sonra",
            "üş",
            "ümüz",
            "den"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "dön",
            "üş",
            "ümüz",
            "den",
            "sonra"
          ],
          "explanation": "dön + üş + ümüz + den + sonra. Our is -ümüz, your would be -ünüz."
        },
        {
          "id": "3",
          "ru": "from the start of the meeting on",
          "lead": "toplantının",
          "pool": [
            "sonra",
            "ma",
            "başla",
            "ndan",
            "sı",
            "itibaren"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "başla",
            "ma",
            "sı",
            "ndan",
            "itibaren"
          ],
          "explanation": "“From the start on” is itibaren, not sonra."
        },
        {
          "id": "4",
          "ru": "before you leave",
          "lead": "senin",
          "pool": [
            "iş",
            "önce",
            "git",
            "in",
            "gid",
            "den"
          ],
          "answer": [
            "gid",
            "iş",
            "in",
            "den",
            "önce"
          ],
          "explanation": "git + iş = gidiş: t softens before a vowel. Your is -in."
        }
      ]
    },
